;;;;;; Martini lipid topology for C16:0/16:1 LE (PYLE), generated using:
; The Martini lipid itp generator version M3.l01  Args are: -alname PYLE -alhead 'E P' -allink 'G L' -altail 'cCDC cCCC'
; WARNING: Autogenerated and not all lipid headgroup and tail combinations have been tested;
;          used with care and see K.B. Pedersen et al. 2024 for guidance.
;
; Description:
;   A general model plasmalogen phosphatidylethanolamine (LE) lipid corresponding to atomistic C16:0/16:1(9c) 1-palmitoyl-2-palmitoleoyl tails.
; Parameterization:
;   This topology follows the standard Martini 3.0 lipid definitions and building block rules. 
;   Bonded parameters and mapping have been optimized as described in K.B. Pedersen et al. 2024.
; Reference(s): 
; K.B. Pedersen et al., The Martini 3 Lipidome: Expanded and Refined Parameters Improve Lipid Phase Behavior*, 
; ACS Central Science, 2025. doi: 10.1021/acscentsci.5c00755
; P.C.T. Souza et al., Martini 3: A General Purpose Force Field for Coarse-Grained Molecular Dynamics*, 
; Nature Methods, 2021. doi: 10.1038/s41592-021-01098-3
; Created: 2024.07.12
;
; Molecular topology and mapping of indices:
; NH3-PO4-GL1-C1A-C2A-D3A-C4A
;          |
;         PL2-C1B-C2B-C3B-C4B
;
;  1 - 2 - 3 - 5 - 6 - 7 - 8 
;          |
;          4 - 9 - 10- 11- 12
;
;@INSANE alhead=E P, allink=G L, altail=CCDC CCCC, alname=PYLE, charge=0.0
;@RESNTEST PYL==PYLE if: atoms[0]==NH3
;@BEADS NH3 PO4 GL1 PL2 C1A C2A D3A C4A C1B C2B C3B C4B 
;@BONDS NH3-PO4 PO4-GL1 PO4-PL2 GL1-PL2 GL1-C1A C1A-C2A C2A-D3A D3A-C4A PL2-C1B C1B-C2B C2B-C3B C3B-C4B 
;

